      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.I need to find the `TestingField` class used in the test.Let me look at the original `TestDayOfYear.java` to find `TestingField`.Let me read the full `TestingField` implementation from the original test.Let me check the compile script and test-classes directory to understand the build setup.Now I have all the context I need. The original file references `TestingField.INSTANCE` but never defines it — I need to include it as a private inner class (just like in `TestDayOfYear.java`). I'll also remove the many unused imports and unused constants to improve understandability.The improved test compiles successfully. The key understandability improvements made were:\n\n1. **Removed ~40 unused imports** — only the 9 actually needed imports remain.\n2. **Removed unused constants** (`YEAR_STANDARD`, `YEAR_LEAP`, `STANDARD_YEAR_LENGTH`, `LEAP_YEAR_LENGTH`, `PARIS`) that cluttered the class.\n3. **Added `TestingField` inner class** — the original file referenced `TestingField.INSTANCE` without ever defining it; the class is now included with a brief Javadoc explaining its purpose.\n4. **Added a short comment** on `test_getLong_derivedField` explaining the non-obvious delegation path being exercised."
